l, it becomes needs_evidence. Never turn it into a pass.\n18\tIf absent, use verdict upheld; if unclear, use verdict unclear.\n19\t\n20\t\n21\t## E07.1\n22\t\n23\t**Check:** Every peer message is authenticated to a specific sending agent, even when the message is validly signed.\n24\t\n25\t**How to verify:** 1) Find the handler for incoming peer messages (A2A server, peer endpoint). 2) Check each message is authenticated to a specific sending agent (mTLS identity, verified token subject). 3) Answer no if any route accepts unauthenticated messages, trusts a self-declared sender field, or accepts any valid signature without mapping it to a known agent.\n26\t\n27\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n28\t\n29\t**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no A2A or peer-agent endpoint; /ingest/mail and /slack/interactions are signed gateway and human channels.\n30\t\n31\t(no evidence cited)\n32\t\n33\t## E07.2\n34\t\n35\t**Check:** Message types and schemas are validated, and each request is checked against what that peer is allowed to ask for, including tenant.\n36\t\n37\t**How to verify:** 1) Open the peer message handler. 2) Check message type and schema validation. 3) Check a per-peer allowlist of request types and tenants, keyed on the authenticated sender. 4) Answer no if schemas are unchecked, any authenticated peer can ask for anything, or tenant is taken from the message body.\n38\t\n39\t**Reviewer's evidence:**  — \"\"\n40\t\n41\t**Reviewer's note:** N/A candidate: no peer message handler.\n42\t\n43\t(no evidence cited)\n44\t\n45\t## E07.3\n46\t\n47\t**Check:** Action requests carry a nonce or request ID and a freshness check, and replays are rejected or do not repeat side effects.\n48\t\n49\t**How to verify:** 1) Find action request handling. 2) Check for a nonce or request ID plus a freshness (timestamp) check, with seen IDs stored. 3) Answer no if no replay check exists, the nonce is never stored or compared, or a repeated ID repeats side effects.\n50\t\n51\t**Reviewer